  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-year funding to the Occupied Palestinian Territories&apos; Humanitarian Fund (2026-2029).</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To provide funding to UN/OCHA&#x2019;s Occupied Palestinian Territory-Humanitarian Fund (OPT HF), the Country&#x2013;Based Pooled Fund (CBPF), in Palestine. 
OPT HF aims to ensure that humanitarian needs are addressed in a collaborative manner, fostering cooperation and coordination within and between clusters and humanitarian organisations. The OPT HF contributes to improving needs assessments, enhancing the Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) as the strategic planning document for humanitarian action, strengthening coordination mechanisms, in particular the cluster system, and improving accountability through an enhanced monitoring and reporting framework. Interventions supported by the OPT HF are to be consistent with the core humanitarian principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence. The OPT HF is primarily aligned to support the delivery of strategic humanitarian response identified under the HRP while retaining the flexibility to allocate funds to unforeseen events or special requirements.</narrative>
  </description>
